## 5. Stakeholder Information Needs

Different stakeholder groups require different information to understand, validate, or act on the current-state assessment.

The assessment should provide information appropriate to each stakeholder's role while maintaining a consistent evidence-based view of the environment.

| Stakeholder Group | Primary Information Needs |
|---|---|
| Executive Leadership | Consolidated findings, significant risks and gaps, clinical and operational implications, dependencies, unresolved questions, and decision-readiness considerations |
| Clinical Leadership | Clinical workflow dependencies, device criticality, information needs, operational impacts, continuity considerations, and areas requiring further validation |
| Clinical Users | Workflow impacts, information availability, device dependencies, usability considerations, connectivity-related effects, and reported workarounds |
| Clinical Engineering / Biomedical Engineering | Device inventory, lifecycle status, maintenance conditions, vendor support, technical limitations, device dependencies, and security-update considerations |
| IT Infrastructure / Networking | Network connectivity, infrastructure dependencies, security boundaries, monitoring coverage, connectivity risks, and operational support dependencies |
| Integration / Interface Team | Interface relationships, information flows, integration components, ownership, criticality, monitoring, failure dependencies, and unresolved technical questions |
| Cybersecurity | Device exposure, lifecycle and support status, security-update availability, access dependencies, monitoring, existing security evidence, and potential clinical or operational impact |
| EHR / Clinical Systems Team | Relevant system relationships, information exchanged, workflow dependencies, interface relationships, and system-level constraints |
| Vendor / Manufacturer Representatives | Device capabilities, lifecycle and support status, security updates, technical documentation, known limitations, and vendor dependencies |
| Technical Project Manager / Assessment Team | Assessment status, evidence, stakeholder input, assumptions, risks, issues, dependencies, unresolved questions, and decision-readiness information |

Stakeholder information needs may overlap across groups. Where multiple stakeholders require the same information, the assessment should maintain a consistent source of evidence while recognizing that the information may be interpreted differently based on stakeholder responsibilities.

