## 7. Assessment Ownership and Decision Roles

The current-state assessment requires coordination across clinical, technical, operational, cybersecurity, vendor, and leadership stakeholders.

Stakeholder responsibilities should be distinguished from assessment coordination and decision-making responsibilities.

| Role / Stakeholder Group | Assessment Responsibility | Decision Role |
|---|---|---|
| Executive Leadership | Provide organizational priorities, strategic context, and leadership perspective on significant findings and dependencies | Provides organizational direction and decision-making authority for subsequent phases |
| Clinical Leadership | Validate clinical priorities, workflow considerations, clinical criticality, and continuity concerns | Provides clinical leadership perspective and priorities |
| Clinical Users | Describe current workflows, information needs, usability considerations, workarounds, and operational dependencies | Provides practitioner perspective and workflow validation |
| Clinical Engineering / Biomedical Engineering | Validate device inventory, lifecycle, maintenance, technical conditions, and vendor dependencies | Provides technical subject matter expertise regarding devices |
| IT Infrastructure / Networking | Validate network connectivity, infrastructure dependencies, monitoring, and operational support | Provides infrastructure subject matter expertise |
| Integration / Interface Team | Validate interfaces, information flows, integration dependencies, ownership, and monitoring | Provides integration subject matter expertise |
| Cybersecurity | Validate cybersecurity considerations, exposure, access dependencies, monitoring, and available security evidence | Provides cybersecurity subject matter expertise |
| EHR / Clinical Systems Team | Validate relevant clinical-system relationships, information exchange, and workflow dependencies | Provides clinical-system subject matter expertise |
| Vendor / Manufacturer Representatives | Provide product, lifecycle, support, security-update, and technical information when requested | Provides vendor-specific information and clarification |
| Technical Project Manager / Assessment Team | Coordinate assessment activities, evidence collection, stakeholder engagement, risks, assumptions, dependencies, documentation, and decision-readiness activities | Facilitates assessment coordination; does not serve as the technical, clinical, or cybersecurity authority |

The Technical Project Manager / Assessment Team coordinates the assessment process and maintains visibility across stakeholder inputs, evidence, risks, assumptions, issues, and dependencies.

Technical, clinical, operational, and cybersecurity conclusions should be validated by the appropriate subject matter experts rather than assigned solely by the Technical Project Manager / Assessment Team.

Subsequent modernization, procurement, remediation, or implementation decisions are outside the authority of this current-state assessment and would require appropriate leadership and subject matter expert involvement.

